.git
.gitignore
# Secrets reach the API at runtime through env_file, never through an image layer.
**/.env*
!.env.example
*.log
**/.DS_Store
coverage
.vscode
.idea
*.md
!README.md
# The index changelog page and the update check read it.
!CHANGELOG.md
**/node_modules
# Both images build the bundles themselves; a host dist/ would only be stale.
dist/
# Runtime data is bind-mounted at ./data:/app/data — never bake it into the image
# (data/home alone is >1GB and would ship to the daemon on every build).
data*/
apps/api/data
# Caddy's local state (certs, OCSP cache). Bind-mounted, and its churn made every `up --build`
# see a changed context and recreate containers.
caddy-data/
# The image runs the API from source; never ship a stale local bundle.
apps/api/build
apps/index/src/content/.generated/
# Local-only trees the image never reads: backup archives, snapshots, launcher state, agent state, worktrees
# and the docs' screenshots (well over a gigabyte together, all shipped to the daemon on every build).
backups/
snapshots/
.eigen/
.claude/
.superpowers/
.worktrees/
docs/
# Operator files in the install dir: the override may hold inline secrets, and the proxy snippets
# `./eigen setup` writes are for the host web server. The image reads none of them.
docker-compose.override.yml
eigen.nginx.conf
eigen.Caddyfile
eigen.apache.conf
# The Docker harnesses run on the host against a scratch install; the image never reads them.
docker/test-*
docker/probe-lib.sh
